      "repair_reason": "- [P1] Require the contributor to consolidate the shared authorization policy and provide real plugin-runtime Gateway proof; automation cannot supply evidence from the contributor's setup.; Needs attention: The intended boundary is sound, but duplicated authorization policy across session methods creates a concrete future bypass and drift risk.; Review finding: [P1] Consolidate the existing session ownership guard —... (sha=f92235691442bb05cac88e1b2bdf4ff7b3e1600e)",
      "review_summary": "The PR adds plugin-runtime owner checks to session creation and reset paths, persists owner metadata, narrows mismatch error handling, and adds ownership regression coverage.\n\nPR surface: Source +135, Tests +317. Total +452 across 5 files.\n\nReproducibility: no. high-confidence live reproduction was run here, but the current-main source path is clear: sessions.create consumes and can fork a parent without receiving the authenticated plugin owner that sessions.delete checks.",
